<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mangoky River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mangoky is a river in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>, one of the longest on the island at over 500 kilometres. It rises in the central highlands and flows west to a delta on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a> Channel. In the seventeenth century the plains between the Mangoky and the Tsiribihina became the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sakalava">Sakalava</a> kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menabe">Menabe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mangoky-river.jpg" alt="Mangoky River" width="320" height="312" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mangoky_delta.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
